Vendored source
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - plugin/vendor/dbx-plugin-sdk/
    DBX plugin sidecar protocol SDK (`dbx-plugin-sdk` 0.1.0)
    Copyright (c) the DBX authors
    Licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)
    Upstream: https://github.com/t8y2/dbx/tree/main/plugins/sdk/rust/dbx-plugin-sdk
    Vendored at upstream commit cd8f30aa23b11e212c8ab299519ad7bdcd6d16ed.

    Copied into this repository because the SDK is not published on crates.io,
    while the dbx-plugin CLI supports path dependencies. Without a local copy the
    plugin backend could only be built on a machine that happens to have the DBX
    repository checked out beside this one.

    Two local modifications, both confined to Cargo.toml: the empty `[workspace]`
    table was removed so the crate can be a member of this repository's
    workspace, and a `[lints.clippy]` table allows `type_complexity` and
    `items_after_test_module` (CI runs clippy with `-D warnings` over the whole
    workspace, `--exclude` does not suppress lints from a path dependency, and
    adding `#[allow]` inside the source would break the byte-identity guarantee
    below). `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to upstream.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Design lineage
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The architecture and the audio-pipeline design of this project were informed
by the music player subsystem of the VCPChat project
(https://github.com/lioensky/VCPChat), in particular:

  - the three-layer split of audio engine / player / lyric stage;
  - the idea that playback state must have a single authoritative source;
  - the HTTP + WebSocket protocol shape of the audio service.

No source file of that project is copied into this repository. All code here
is an independent implementation written for this project.

The 商籁 (sonnet) lyric visual (`plugin/ui/stanza/stanza-sonnet-fx.js`,
`stanza-sonnet.js`) follows the same rule. Its behaviour — the per-line
cinematic shot selection, the deterministic absolute-time camera paths, the
glyph/phrase typography pipeline, the accent-choreography cueing rules and the
optical-print post-process look — was specified by studying the sonnet stage
mode of VCPChat (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), itself an adaptation of the sonnet
visualizer of the folia project (AGPL-3.0). No source file of either project
is copied into this repository; the implementation, module structure, host
integration and all code are written independently for this project, and the
numeric behaviour contracts are re-expressed against this project's own Stage
facade and stanza theme adapter.

The 汽水音乐 (Soda Music) QR sign-in flow
(`crates/hertz-studio/src/online/qishui.rs`, section "扫码登录") is an independent
Rust implementation. The *protocol facts* it relies on — the Passport Web
endpoint paths, the `aid`, the parameter vocabulary, the status strings and
the `2046` second-verification response — were learned by reading the qishui
authentication bridge of the Mineradio project
(`qishui-qr-login.js`, `qishui-auth-v6.js`), which is licensed
GPL-3.0-only and itself ported from Wx2yZx/Mineradio-Qishui-QR-Login.

No source file of either project is copied into this repository, and no part
of their bdms/sdk-glue runtime is reimplemented: this project's flow uses
plain HTTP only, with no device-fingerprint forgery and no JS challenge
solving. The parameter set was additionally reduced by direct observation of
the live endpoints (see the module documentation), so it differs from the
reference implementation's.

The non-image platform badges in the web UI (`.src-badge` in
`plugin/ui/online.js`) reuse the brand-colour palette of the
Mineradio project's `--source-*` CSS variables. One colour value is not
copyrightable subject matter; it is recorded here for completeness.
